			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Mountain and Vine submodules — Finalize notification delegation to canonical Vine crate\n\n**Mountain** (refactor): Replace the local `super::Notification::*` dispatch with direct calls to `::Vine::Server::Notification::*`, completing the extraction of Cocoon→Mountain IPC logic. All 46+ notification handlers are now thin pass-throughs delegating to the shared Vine library. The `MountainVinegRPCService` is reduced to a pure routing table, with only Mountain-specific utilities (`Support`, `OutputChannelCoalesce`, `TerminalEnvCollection`) retained locally.\n\n**Vine** (refactor): Inline trivial provider unregistration atoms (`UnregisterFileSystemProvider`, `UnregisterUriHandler`) that performed single-step delegation to `UnregisterByHandle`. Retain `UnregisterScmProvider` which contains DJB-31 handle recomputation logic and Sky event relay. Consolidate the unregistration surface to expose only atoms with multi-step orchestration needs.\n\nImpact: Mountain is now a pure composition layer with all Cocoon→Mountain IPC contracts defined canonically in Vine. The provider unregistration pathway is fully symmetrical, and redundant wrapper modules have been eliminated.",
