				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Cache, Mountain, and Vine submodules — Notification delegation completion and provider lifecycle symmetry\n\n**Cache** (docs): Reformat documentation comments in Library.rs to improve readability in source viewers and documentation generators.\n\n**Mountain** (refactor): Complete the systematic decomposition of the gRPC notification surface by delegating all remaining handlers to the Vine crate. Convert `CocoonService` and `MountainService` trait imports to use canonical definitions from `::Vine::Generated`, eliminating local re-exports. The server-side notification modules (`UpdateScmGroup`, `WebviewLifecycle`, `RelayToSky`, provider unregistration) are now thin shims forwarding to `Vine::Server::Notification`. The client-side `Shared` module and stub implementations are reduced to empty pass-throughs, with active code paths using `::Vine::Client::*` directly.\n\n**Vine** (feat): Implement the symmetrical provider unregistration surface — `UnregisterRemoteAuthorityResolver`, `UnregisterScmProvider`, `UnregisterTaskProvider`, and `UnregisterUriHandler` — all integrating with the central `UnregisterByHandle` utility. Add `WebviewLifecycle` notification to canonicalize Cocoon's positional arrays into named-key objects before emitting to Sky renderer channels. Implement `UpdateScmGroup` notification with SCM marker persistence via `VineHost::UpdateScmGroupMarkers` for boot-time replay. Enhance `UnregisterFileSystemProvider` with scheme logging for diagnostic observability.\n\nImpact: Mountain is now a pure composition layer with all Cocoon→Mountain IPC delegated to the shared Vine crate. The provider lifecycle is fully symmetrical with clean disposal pathways, and SCM/webview state persists across page reloads.",
